    "body": "## Security/privacy impact\n\nPublic profile reads previously loaded any user by numeric id, including accounts in `SUSPENDED` state. That left moderation-enforced accounts publicly discoverable and continued exposing profile bio, public location, trust statistics, verification state and service categories after suspension.\n\n## Fix\n\n- add an `id + status` user lookup;\n- resolve public profiles only through `findByIdAndStatus(userId, ACTIVE)`;\n- return the existing neutral user-not-found response for missing and suspended users;\n- ensure suspended users are rejected before review aggregates, completed-job counts, verification state or service categories are read;\n- keep owner profile-edit behavior unchanged, since account self-management uses its existing authenticated path.\n\nNo authentication, payout, wallet, escrow, dispute, job lifecycle or moderation state-transition logic is changed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- active public profiles still expose the existing explicit public fields and trust summary;\n- the active path proves the legacy global `findById` lookup is not used;\n- suspended/missing public profiles fail as not-found before any trust/statistics/verification/category lookup.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks are green on the exact current PR head SHA. Revalidate the exact head and current `master` immediately before merge; if `master` moved, safely rebase/update and rerun checks. Merge with a merge commit guarded by the checked head SHA, then verify the post-merge `master` SHA and all relevant push workflows.",
