          "body": "## Security/privacy impact\n\n`GET /reviews/users/{userId}` is intentionally public, but it still loaded the target through `UserRepository.findById(...)`. After #196 hid suspended public profiles, this left a parallel public surface that could still confirm a suspended numeric user id and expose that account's review history, including completed job titles, reviewer ids/nicknames, ratings and comments.\n\nThat bypassed the moderation privacy boundary introduced for `/users/{id}/profile`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve public review targets only through `findByIdAndStatus(userId, ACTIVE)`, reusing the same active-account boundary as public profiles;\n- return the existing neutral user-not-found response for missing and suspended accounts;\n- stop before querying `ReviewRepository` when the target is not publicly visible;\n- preserve review creation, bilateral accountability, participant-only eligibility, block behavior and all stored review records unchanged;\n- keep active users' public review pages unchanged.\n\nNo review deletion, moderation state transition, notification behavior, escrow/payment flow or authenticated participant authorization is changed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- unit coverage proves active public reviews use the ACTIVE-scoped user lookup and do not fall back to global `findById`;\n- suspended/missing targets fail before any public review query;\n- `Reviews trust smoke` still verifies bilateral review creation, duplicate protection, trust aggregates and public active reviews;\n- the same runtime smoke then suspends a reviewed user in the database and requires both `/users/{id}/profile` and `/reviews/users/{id}` to return neutral `404`.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head SHA are green. Revalidate the exact head, review threads and current `master` immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it and rerun checks. Merge with a merge commit guarded by the checked head SHA, then verify the merge parents and every post-merge push workflow before starting another slice.",
